.swiftpm/
# Written by `Starkit registry` — and by C6 on every save — into whichever STARKIT_HOME it was
# pointed at, which is seed/ when a measurement runs against a scratch install. The one that is used
# is in ~/.starkit, and install.sh regenerates it there on every run — nothing vendors this copy.
seed/src/registry.gleam

# Per home as well, and written by the same scratch runs: `Starkit describe` refreshes the Catalogue's
# cache, and a build behind it records what it compiled. Neither is seed content — Seeding.verdict
# would not carry them anyway — and both name one machine's Scripts.
seed/manifests.json
seed/built.json
